"note": "@luis_pereira87 I will fix the QFI handling for downlink packets \u2014 that is a legitimate bug and is in scope for the simple-switch flavour.\n\nHowever, full QoS enforcement (QFI-based classification, per-flow shaping, MBR/GBR, QER application, etc.) is not planned for simple-switch. That feature set is fully implemented, tested, and validated on the eBPF UPF \u2014 including interop testing against several core network providers (Free5GC, Open5GS, OAI, Keysight) and against TRex with a mocked SMF \u2014 and the eBPF flavour is our reference datapath for any QoS-sensitive deployment.\n\nOut of curiosity, is there a specific blocker preventing you from using the eBPF UPF? If there is something we can help unblock, please let us know \u2014 it would be the most direct path forward and you would get the full QoS feature set out of the box.\n\nIf eBPF is genuinely not an option in your setup and QoS enforcement on simple-switch is a hard requirement on your side, please open an official feature request. Implementing and validating full QoS on simple-switch is a substantial piece of work and needs to be scoped, prioritized, and tracked properly rather than addressed inside this issue.\n\nKind regards, \n\nFrancky",
"note_html": "<p data-sourcepos=\"1:1-1:140\" dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"/luis_pereira87\" title=\"Luis Pereira\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" data-user=\"9684\" data-original=\"@luis_pereira87\" data-container=\"body\" data-placement=\"top\" data-reference-type=\"user\">@luis_pereira87</a> I will fix the QFI handling for downlink packets \u2014 that is a legitimate bug and is in scope for the simple-switch flavour.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"3:1-3:440\" dir=\"auto\">However, full QoS enforcement (QFI-based classification, per-flow shaping, MBR/GBR, QER application, etc.) is not planned for simple-switch. That feature set is fully implemented, tested, and validated on the eBPF UPF \u2014 including interop testing against several core network providers (Free5GC, Open5GS, OAI, Keysight) and against TRex with a mocked SMF \u2014 and the eBPF flavour is our reference datapath for any QoS-sensitive deployment.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"5:1-5:251\" dir=\"auto\">Out of curiosity, is there a specific blocker preventing you from using the eBPF UPF? If there is something we can help unblock, please let us know \u2014 it would be the most direct path forward and you would get the full QoS feature set out of the box.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"7:1-7:346\" dir=\"auto\">If eBPF is genuinely not an option in your setup and QoS enforcement on simple-switch is a hard requirement on your side, please open an official feature request. Implementing and validating full QoS on simple-switch is a substantial piece of work and needs to be scoped, prioritized, and tracked properly rather than addressed inside this issue.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"9:1-9:14\" dir=\"auto\">Kind regards,</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"11:1-11:7\" dir=\"auto\">Francky</p>",
"body_first_line_html": "<p><a href=\"/luis_pereira87\" title=\"Luis Pereira\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" data-user=\"9684\" data-reference-type=\"user\">@luis_pereira87</a> I will fix the QFI handling for downlink packets \u2014 that is a legitimate bug and is in scope for the simple...</p>",
