"external_author": null,
"note": "Hi, \n\nI'm not able to reproduce this on my release \u2014 DL traffic comes out with QFI = 1 as provisioned.\n\nRepro per Luis' simplified steps (CN + gNB + UE in RFsim), then DL-only traffic with no prior UL:\n\n```\n$ docker exec -it oai-ext-dn ping 12.1.1.2\nPING 12.1.1.2 (12.1.1.2) 56(84) bytes of data.\n64 bytes from 12.1.1.2: icmp_seq=1 ttl=64 time=1.20 ms\n64 bytes from 12.1.1.2: icmp_seq=2 ttl=64 time=1.27 ms\n...\n```\n\nNo `Dropping UL SDAP PDU with unmapped QFI=5` on the RAN side.\n\nProvisioning (single non-GBR flow, 5QI 5):\n\n```\ndecision_supi1:\n  supi_imsi: \"208950000000031\"\n  pcc_rules:\n    - non-gbr-rule-5qi-5\n\nnon-gbr-rule-5qi-5:\n  flowInfos:\n    - flowDescription: permit out icmp from any to 12.1.1.0/24\n  packetFilterUsage: true\n  precedence: 20\n  refQosData:\n    - non-gbr-qos-5qi-5\n\nnon-gbr-qos-5qi-5:\n  5qi: 5\n  arp:\n    priorityLevel: 8\n    preemptCap: NOT_PREEMPT\n    preemptVuln: PREEMPTABLE\n```\n\nSMF log:\n\n```\n[smf_app] [debug] Successfully associate PDR 1 with F-TEID ID 0x1 - IP: 192.168.71.129 (QFI: 1)\n```\n\nI've attached the capture (`traffic_simple_switch.pcapng`). Decoding the DL GTP-U packets:\n\n* GTP-U `T-PDU`, TEID 1, next-ext-header `0x85` (PDU Session Container)\n* PDU Session Container: **PDU type = DL, QFI = 1**\n\nSo on my build the UPF preserves the SMF/PFCP-provisioned QFI on DL even with no preceding UL packet \u2014 i.e. `session->qfi` is not falling back to the 0x05 default.\n\nGiven that, could you share the exact release/branch + commit (and the simple-switch UPF image/tag) used in the failing runs? I'd like to align on the same revision so I can either confirm a fix already landed or repro against the version where you're seeing QFI=5.\n\n[traffic_simple_switch.pcapng](/uploads/c0e1bdaefac07f3ef56390c6db09d179/traffic_simple_switch.pcapng)",
"note_html": "<p data-sourcepos=\"1:1-1:4\" dir=\"auto\">Hi,</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"3:1-3:98\" dir=\"auto\">I'm not able to reproduce this on my release \u2014 DL traffic comes out with QFI = 1 as provisioned.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"5:1-5:97\" dir=\"auto\">Repro per Luis' simplified steps (CN + gNB + UE in RFsim), then DL-only traffic with no prior UL:</p>\n<div class=\"gl-relative markdown-code-block js-markdown-code\"><pre data-sourcepos=\"7:1-13:3\" class=\"code highlight js-syntax-highlight language-plaintext\" v-pre=\"true\"><code><span id=\"LC1\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">$ docker exec -it oai-ext-dn ping 12.1.1.2</span>\n<span id=\"LC2\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">PING 12.1.1.2 (12.1.1.2) 56(84) bytes of data.</span>\n<span id=\"LC3\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">64 bytes from 12.1.1.2: icmp_seq=1 ttl=64 time=1.20 ms</span>\n<span id=\"LC4\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">64 bytes from 12.1.1.2: icmp_seq=2 ttl=64 time=1.27 ms</span>\n<span id=\"LC5\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">...</span></code></pre><copy-code></copy-code><insert-code-snippet></insert-code-snippet></div>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"15:1-15:62\" dir=\"auto\">No <code data-sourcepos=\"15:4-15:45\">Dropping UL SDAP PDU with unmapped QFI=5</code> on the RAN side.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"17:1-17:42\" dir=\"auto\">Provisioning (single non-GBR flow, 5QI 5):</p>\n<div class=\"gl-relative markdown-code-block js-markdown-code\"><pre data-sourcepos=\"19:1-39:3\" class=\"code highlight js-syntax-highlight language-plaintext\" v-pre=\"true\"><code><span id=\"LC1\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">decision_supi1:</span>\n<span id=\"LC2\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">  supi_imsi: \"208950000000031\"</span>\n<span id=\"LC3\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">  pcc_rules:</span>\n<span id=\"LC4\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">    - non-gbr-rule-5qi-5</span>\n<span id=\"LC5\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\"></span>\n<span id=\"LC6\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">non-gbr-rule-5qi-5:</span>\n<span id=\"LC7\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">  flowInfos:</span>\n<span id=\"LC8\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">    - flowDescription: permit out icmp from any to 12.1.1.0/24</span>\n<span id=\"LC9\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">  packetFilterUsage: true</span>\n<span id=\"LC10\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">  precedence: 20</span>\n<span id=\"LC11\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">  refQosData:</span>\n<span id=\"LC12\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">    - non-gbr-qos-5qi-5</span>\n<span id=\"LC13\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\"></span>\n<span id=\"LC14\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">non-gbr-qos-5qi-5:</span>\n<span id=\"LC15\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">  5qi: 5</span>\n<span id=\"LC16\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">  arp:</span>\n<span id=\"LC17\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">    priorityLevel: 8</span>\n<span id=\"LC18\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">    preemptCap: NOT_PREEMPT</span>\n<span id=\"LC19\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">    preemptVuln: PREEMPTABLE</span></code></pre><copy-code></copy-code><insert-code-snippet></insert-code-snippet></div>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"41:1-41:8\" dir=\"auto\">SMF log:</p>\n<div class=\"gl-relative markdown-code-block js-markdown-code\"><pre data-sourcepos=\"43:1-45:3\" class=\"code highlight js-syntax-highlight language-plaintext\" v-pre=\"true\"><code><span id=\"LC1\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">[smf_app] [debug] Successfully associate PDR 1 with F-TEID ID 0x1 - IP: 192.168.71.129 (QFI: 1)</span></code></pre><copy-code></copy-code><insert-code-snippet></insert-code-snippet></div>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"47:1-47:90\" dir=\"auto\">I've attached the capture (<code data-sourcepos=\"47:28-47:57\">traffic_simple_switch.pcapng</code>). Decoding the DL GTP-U packets:</p>\n<ul data-sourcepos=\"49:1-50:51\" dir=\"auto\">\n<li data-sourcepos=\"49:1-49:71\">GTP-U <code data-sourcepos=\"49:9-49:15\">T-PDU</code>, TEID 1, next-ext-header <code data-sourcepos=\"49:42-49:47\">0x85</code> (PDU Session Container)</li>\n<li data-sourcepos=\"50:1-50:51\">PDU Session Container: <strong data-sourcepos=\"50:26-50:51\">PDU type = DL, QFI = 1</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"52:1-52:165\" dir=\"auto\">So on my build the UPF preserves the SMF/PFCP-provisioned QFI on DL even with no preceding UL packet \u2014 i.e. <code data-sourcepos=\"52:111-52:124\">session-&gt;qfi</code> is not falling back to the 0x05 default.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"54:1-54:265\" dir=\"auto\">Given that, could you share the exact release/branch + commit (and the simple-switch UPF image/tag) used in the failing runs? I'd like to align on the same revision so I can either confirm a fix already landed or repro against the version where you're seeing QFI=5.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"56:1-56:102\" dir=\"auto\"><a data-sourcepos=\"56:1-56:102\" href=\"https://gitlab.eurecom.fr/-/project/5331/uploads/c0e1bdaefac07f3ef56390c6db09d179/traffic_simple_switch.pcapng\" data-canonical-src=\"/uploads/c0e1bdaefac07f3ef56390c6db09d179/traffic_simple_switch.pcapng\" data-link=\"true\" class=\"gfm\">traffic_simple_switch.pcapng</a></p>",
"body_first_line_html": "<p>Hi,...</p>",
